core-v-verif: fixes for slang (svcheck corpus core-v-cv32e40p)

What the simulators the bench targets accept and slang 11 rejects as
errors. Each change keeps the bench's meaning.

- uvma_obi_memory drv/mon: a virtual interface variable with a modport is
  assigned the virtual interface itself (IEEE 1800-2017 25.9: one with no
  modport may be assigned to one with a modport), not `vif.<modport>`,
  which slang does not take as an expression.
- uvmt_cv32e40p_rvvi_if: the interface ports interrupt_if and debug_if
  become an input for the one signal it reads (debug_if.debug_req). slang
  refuses an interface with interface ports as a virtual interface, and the
  coverage models hold this one as one.
- uvme_rv32x_hwloop_covg: `get_coverage()` with its parentheses; slang
  requires them on a built-in method call.

The solve-before inside a foreach (uvma_interrupt_seq_item, 18.5.10) is
left as it is; tests/corpora/core-v-cv32e40p.f downgrades it.

